Z||000008||DXR_DAD||07-03-2000||06:28 PM||||Gokart, I'm Back and that looks GOOOOOOOD!!<BR>from the pics I can tell you are happy with it?,  That shot looks just like the one I took of mine. I put a thin strip of rubber<BR>around the bottom, but you can't see it, it's to stop any water from seeping in.<P>GOOD JOB!!<P>DR_DAD||||reg||14
Z||000009||dogtired||07-03-2000||08:20 PM||||The rubber strip you folks are talking about?? is that along the right and left side of the scoop, between the scoop and deck lid???    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>What type of rubber did you use??? I do not think I will mold mine into the deck lid at this time, Please let me know. Rubber sounds like a good idea??<BR>I purchased one of Toms scoops about a month ago and haven't gotten it installed yet??<BR>I was thinking about putting some 1/4 to 1/2 inch square screen wire, maybe brass in the inlet just to keep trash and stuff out? What do you think?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I really do not want to stuff foam rubber in it every time I park the car, or every night cause it might rain?<BR>Yours looks Great, that is why I bought one. THANKS TOM!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by dogtired (edited 07-03-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000010||DXR_DAD||07-03-2000||08:42 PM||||The rubber strip is a door seal, you can get in at Home Depot. You may still want to block off the scoop opening with foam rubber<BR>when it rains!! just to keep the water off the engine, (over night and while driving in the rain). Not a lot of trash gets in, just don't park under any trees or stuff like that<BR>If you want to you could put the screen over the hole in the deck lid, not the opening of the scoop, this is what I might do. If you put the screen in the scoop opening you can't block it off with the foam to keep the water out. Blocking off the opening with foam is the best way I found to keep the water out<BR>and it doesn't look bad at all!! when you drive with it on. If any of you guys find another way please let us know.<P>DXR_DAD||||reg||14
Z||000011||webbee||07-03-2000||09:10 PM||||You gould get 1/8 stainless steal hardware cloth and fiberglass it in to keep crap out. Won't help much with rain though. Available at marine supply. By the way what's rain?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> (A So. CA joke!) <P>Really nice job Go Kart, just a first class job.<p>[This message has been edited by webbee (edited 07-03-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000012||Coconut||07-03-2000||09:38 PM||||WOW,<BR>That is really sharp looking. I'm gonna have to add one of those to my car. Another mod to add to the list.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Great looking job guy!<P>webbee~ Rain is the LIQUID version of sunshine   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> (WA.joke!) Lord knows, we get LOTS of that!<P>Cruisin' On,<BR>Coconut <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Larry's_Signature_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by Coconut (edited 07-03-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||Gokart||07-03-2000||09:43 PM||||Thanks DAD! Glad you approve and YES I'm tickled with the results! Had a hell of a time paiting it so when I get Mechams their going to a bodyshop. I just went with the instructions you gave me and that are on <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroproject.com</A>  and used 1/4 inch fuel line hose for a gasket around the opening I cut for the scoop. I spliced it down and fit it around the edges and then used high heat rtv around it on both sides. Unless I'm spraying water directly into scoop, no water enters the engine area! I even wash my car without foam blocking opening and the plenum is dry as a bone after. Maybe I cut my hole a little smaller than most? I cut the hole 17" across and 11" up and down. Good luck when you do yours dog and were here to help. I like the chances that trash won't enter the scoop so I not going to be too concerned about it. Anyways WE LOVE IT! Thanks Tom <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>------------------<BR> Marc                     87GT||||reg||14
Z||000014||webbee||07-03-2000||09:52 PM||||GOKART was on your web site and when I went to the 6x9 install in dash article the instructions come up but there was no pic. Should there be? <P>COCONUT At the risk of starting a can-nuk convention on this thread, I used to live in Vancouver, B.C. I know all about that liquid sunshine.||||reg||1
